// A library that reads part of the record it is handed.
//
// Neither function names the whole record, and nothing here can: the value that
// arrives is built by whichever module calls these, and that module is not this
// one. Width subtyping is what lets the interface be the record rather than the
// two numbers a caller would otherwise have to unpack for it.

open import "blot:prelude"

return {
  .zoom_of = fn camera => camera.zoom;
  .doubled = fn camera => camera.zoom * 2;
  }
